{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793448969,"nonce":"u5Nq6jKmA25BBqin6R6PpKZ8RLA=","title":"Agent Context Protocol: RayDE agents use open-weight models served from GPU actors","message":"Direction from darmie: the GPU session class is not only for streaming framework previews. The same GPU capacity can serve open-weight models, and when RayDE builds the Agent Context Protocol feature its agents connect to those GPU actors. Not scheduled; this records what the earlier GPU work should leave room for.\n\nHow it maps onto what exists:\n- A model server is a long-lived actor on dynASB (GPU microVM, Venus), reached through nan8's sandbox API and Reflow, not a session. Token output fits StreamHub events (JSON, sequenced, resumable); embeddings or audio would use the byte streams added in dynASB's binary path.\n- Entitlement: native/sync Entitlement.gpu_ms_per_period (5abd43d) already meters GPU time apart from storage. Preview rendering and inference both draw on it; whether they get separate allowances is a pricing decision.\n- Scheduling is nan8's (6cea173): GPU pool placement, and keeping a loaded model warm instead of reloading weights per request.\n- Weights are large and shared: read-only volumes mounted into many actors, snapshots of a loaded model for fast start. The sandbox API's volumes and snapshots (nan8 docs/sandbox-api.md) are the hook; sizes far above today's volume minimum.\n- Network: a model actor needs no egress; an agent session that calls it does. Allowlists stay with the backend that enforces them (MSB), and the agent reaches the model through nan8, not directly.\n- Tenancy and abuse: per-tenant concurrency and token or GPU-time quotas belong in nan8's metering (d942951).\n\nOpen for when it is built:\n- What the protocol carries between a RayDE agent and a model actor: prompts and tools over MCP (aab3b7c) or a RayDE-specific context protocol, and who owns tool execution.\n- Which open-weight runtimes the GPU actor image supports, and whether Venus performance is enough for inference or needs passthrough on a dedicated node.\n- Context the agent sends from the workspace (files, diagnostics, selection) and what may leave the session.","files":null}]}